{"availability":"available","full":"google/magika","name":"magika","description":"Fast and accurate AI powered file content types detection ","category":"Education","language":"Rust","stars":18701,"forks":1174,"created":"2023-08-22T09:36:55Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:18:52Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://securityresearch.google/magika/","topics":["ai","deep-learning","filetype","keras-classification-models","keras-models","mime-types","onnx"],"demo":"https://securityresearch.google/magika/demo/magika-demo/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.722Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.722Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.722Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.722Z","stars":18701,"forks":1174}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Magika is a novel AI-powered file type detection tool that relies on the recent advance of deep learning to provide accurate detection. Under the hood, Magika employs a custom, highly optimized model that only weighs about a few MBs, and enables precise file identification within milliseconds, even when running on a single CPU. Magika has been trained and evaluated on a dataset of 100M samples across 200+ content types (covering both binary and textual file formats), and it achieves an average 99% accuracy on our test set.","Here is an example of what Magika command line output looks like:","Magika is used at scale to help improve Google users' safety by routing Gmail, Drive, and Safe Browsing files to the proper security and content policy scanners, processing hundreds billions samples on a weekly basis. Magika has also been integrated with VirusTotal (example) and abuse.ch (example)."],"features":["Available as a command line tool written in Rust, a Python API, and additional bindings for Rust, JavaScript/TypeScript (with an experimental npm package, which powers our web demo), and GoLang (WIP).","Trained and evaluated on a dataset of 100M files across 200+ content types.","On our test set, Magika achieves 99% average precision and recall, outperforming existing approaches -- especially on textual content types.","After the model is loaded (which is a one-off overhead), the inference time is about 5ms per file, even when run on a single CPU.","You can invoke Magika with even thousands of files at the same time. You can also use -r for recursively scanning a directory."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/google/magika/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cbae2ed41163d1885cec361c5478aeba7691afa821ac082905812aac827e7722","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.810Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.810Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Magika is a novel AI-powered file type detection tool that relies on the recent advance of deep learning to provide accurate detection. Under the hood, Magika employs a custom, highly optimized model that only weighs about a few MBs, and enables precise file identification within milliseconds, even when running on a single CPU. Magika has been trained and evaluated on a dataset of 100M samples across 200+ content types (covering both binary and textual file formats), and it achieves an average 99% accuracy on our test set.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/google/magika/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"cbae2ed41163d1885cec361c5478aeba7691afa821ac082905812aac827e7722","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/google/magika/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:34.810Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T15:18:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/google/magika/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T23:13:05.259Z","hash":"cbae2ed41163d1885cec361c5478aeba7691afa821ac082905812aac827e7722","originalBytes":10339,"storedBytes":10339,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["magika","content","python","file","type","shell","code","prints","data","text","about"